  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Education, crop diversification and food security for Q&apos;eqchi&apos; communities in Fray Bartolom de las Casas, Alta Verapaz</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Young women in the municipality of Fray Bartolome de las Casas in Alta Verapaz have very limited educational opportunities and their families often face shortages of food supply. Asociaci&amp;oacute;n de Mujeres Adelina Caal Maqu&amp;iacute;n (ACM) runs a community high school and provides technical assistance to develop skills in diversifying crops and protecting natural resources. At the IAF we support community-led solutions to expand economic opportunity in Guatemala. ACM&amp;#39;s activities promote smallholder agriculture and food production to enhance food security and ensure meaningful opportunities for communities to thrive. This grant is part of the IAF&amp;#39;s efforts to address the root causes of irregular migration in Central America.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;</narrative>
  </description>
